In This topic we will cover the concept of Panic Atttack!!

some information:
1. Panic attacks are sudden, intense episodes of fear or anxiety.
2. Symptoms include rapid heart rate, difficulty breathing, and dizziness.
3. They can happen without warning or an obvious cause.
4. Frequent attacks may lead to panic disorder, where there's a constant fear of future episodes.

Data Transformation steps:
1. In the dataset, we need to add a new column named "panic_attack(HML)". 
   This column will categorize the existing "panic_attack" column values into three levels: High, Medium, and Low.
2. It has been identified that the values in the "Heart_rate" column were recorded incorrectly. To correct this, 
  we will use the "standard" measure in Power BI to subtract 1 from each value in the "Heart_rate" column.


Column,Description,Example Values
ID,Unique patient identifier,"1, 2, ..., 1200"
Age,Patient's age at time of record,18–64
Gender,Patient gender,"Female, Male, Non-binary"
Panic_Attack_Frequency,Number of panic attacks reported (0–9 scale),"0, 5, 9"
Duration_Minutes,Length of the panic attack in minutes,5–44
Trigger,Identified trigger for the attack,"Caffeine, PTSD, Stress, Unknown"
Heart_Rate,Heart rate during the attack (note: requires correction—see below),80–159
Sweating,Presence of sweating (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Shortness_of_Breath,Presence of shortness of breath (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Dizziness,Presence of dizziness (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Chest_Pain,Presence of chest pain (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Trembling,Presence of trembling (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Medical_History,Pre-existing conditions,"Anxiety, PTSD, Depression, None"
Medication,Currently on medication (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Caffeine_Intake,Daily caffeine intake (cups),0–5
Exercise_Frequency,Weekly exercise sessions,0–6
Sleep_Hours,Average nightly sleep hours,4.0–9.0
Alcohol_Consumption,Weekly alcohol units,0–9
Smoking,Smoking status (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Therapy,Currently in therapy (Yes/No),"Yes, No"
Panic_Score,Overall severity score (1–10),1–10
